# Build configuration for OpenConnectMenu.
#
#   cp config.env.example config.env     then fill in at least TEAM_ID and BUNDLE_ID
#
# config.env is ignored by git: these values are your own.
# Any variable can also be passed through the environment, which takes precedence over this file:
#   NOTARY_PROFILE=my-profile ./build.sh pkg

# --- Required ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Team ID of the Apple developer account: 10 characters
# (developer.apple.com/account, "Membership details" section).
TEAM_ID=ABCDE12345

# Bundle identifier of the app, in reverse-DNS notation. The helper's is derived from it
# (<BUNDLE_ID>.helper), as is the package's (<BUNDLE_ID>.pkg).
BUNDLE_ID=com.example.OpenConnectMenu

# --- Optional ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Signing identities. By default, build.sh looks in your keychain for the
# "Developer ID Application" and "Developer ID Installer" certificates of your TEAM_ID. Set them if there
# are several; list them with: security find-identity -v
#IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: First Last (ABCDE12345)"
#INSTALLER_IDENTITY="Developer ID Installer: First Last (ABCDE12345)"

# notarytool profile (xcrun notarytool store-credentials). Without it, the package is signed but not
# notarized. Setting it here notarizes EVERY package built; prefer passing it when needed:
#   NOTARY_PROFILE=my-profile ./build.sh pkg
#NOTARY_PROFILE=

# macOS configuration profile: name of the file profiles/<name>.env (template: profiles/example.env)
# that defines the settings ./build.sh mobileconfig enforces on the app (server, authentication group…).
# It is only used by the mobileconfig command; the app package stays the same for everyone.
#PROFILE=
